WEBVTT

00:04.385 --> 00:06.428
Another grueling day.

00:06.887 --> 00:08.930
I just wanna go home
and do nothing.

00:12.476 --> 00:15.061
K-Koichi…

00:15.521 --> 00:17.105
Hazamada…

00:17.607 --> 00:19.317
Hey, what's new?

00:19.692 --> 00:22.277
Th-Thanks again for the other day.

00:23.696 --> 00:26.407
Um, are you all better now?

00:26.949 --> 00:28.283
Sorta, I guess.

00:28.451 --> 00:30.286
They sent me home two days ago.

00:32.663 --> 00:35.248
Where's that bastard—
I mean, where's Josuke?

00:35.416 --> 00:37.084
He already went home.

00:37.251 --> 00:40.337
Supposedly he found an
invisible baby yesterday,

00:40.588 --> 00:43.132
and there was this big
to-do over finding its mother.

00:43.674 --> 00:45.300
So it's a Stand user?

00:45.593 --> 00:46.510
It would seem.

00:47.094 --> 00:51.264
Apparently, the baby bonded
with Josuke's dad, Mr. Joestar.

00:51.390 --> 00:55.890
In fact, without Mr. Joestar close by,
she turns everything around her invisible.

00:57.605 --> 01:01.025
So is Mr. Joestar gonna stick
around here for a while, then?

01:01.525 --> 01:02.651
Seems likely.

01:03.402 --> 01:04.152
I see.

01:04.612 --> 01:07.323
Hey, Koichi, ya like manga?

01:07.448 --> 01:08.198
Manga?

01:08.407 --> 01:10.951
I guess I like comics
as much as the next guy.

01:11.285 --> 01:14.788
Ever heard of Rohan Kishibe,
the guy who draws <i>Pink Dark Boy?</i>

01:14.955 --> 01:17.207
<i>Pink Dark Boy?</i> Of course!

01:17.500 --> 01:18.667
I'm a huge fan!

01:18.918 --> 01:20.419
Really? You like it?

01:20.544 --> 01:22.212
The suspense-horror series, right?

01:22.338 --> 01:24.840
It can get pretty gross,

01:24.924 --> 01:26.675
but that spine-tingling
sense of looming dread…

01:26.801 --> 01:29.470
and those super realistic characters…
aren't they great?

01:29.679 --> 01:31.013
Yeah, yeah!

01:31.263 --> 01:35.642
Did you know Rohan Kishibe
lives right here in Morioh?

01:35.810 --> 01:36.560
Huh?!

01:36.769 --> 01:39.104
What?! He lives in Morioh?!

01:39.605 --> 01:41.607
No way!
You can't be serious! Really?!

01:41.732 --> 01:43.692
I couldn't believe it, either!

01:43.901 --> 01:46.820
I overheard some realtors talking.

01:46.904 --> 01:50.073
It's mind-boggling,
I know, but it's true!

01:50.908 --> 01:53.702
MORIOH STATION

01:53.911 --> 01:56.079
ROHAN KISHIBE'S HOUSE

01:54.120 --> 01:56.038
Hell yeah! I'm there!

01:58.833 --> 02:00.501
You and I, we really get each other.

02:00.710 --> 02:01.794
Really?

02:02.086 --> 02:03.587
KISHIBE

02:04.046 --> 02:04.796
There!

02:04.922 --> 02:07.049
I think that might be his studio.

02:07.299 --> 02:08.258
The light's on!

02:08.342 --> 02:09.801
You're right…

02:10.094 --> 02:12.471
I wonder if he has any family.

02:12.680 --> 02:14.556
I heard he lives alone.

02:14.640 --> 02:17.392
He made his debut at sixteen,
and now he's twenty.

02:17.518 --> 02:20.145
Twenty?! He's so young!

02:20.855 --> 02:23.399
So he was about
my age when he went pro…

02:23.607 --> 02:28.107
KISHIBE

02:23.691 --> 02:26.527
It's no use snooping around, Koichi.

02:26.986 --> 02:28.195
Just ring the doorbell.

02:28.279 --> 02:29.905
M-Me?

02:30.197 --> 02:33.200
Do it! I have seniority over you!

02:33.367 --> 02:35.243
This kind of stuff makes me nervous.

02:35.369 --> 02:38.121
What? That's not fair…

02:56.766 --> 03:01.020
EPISODE 14
LET'S GO TO
THE MANGA ARTIST'S HOUSE, PART 1

03:01.645 --> 03:03.271
That face!

03:03.397 --> 03:04.439
Rohan Kishibe!

03:04.732 --> 03:06.024
He looks exactly like his picture

03:06.108 --> 03:08.026
on the cover of that
special New Year's edition!

03:09.612 --> 03:11.447
Uh, I mean… Rohan-sensei!

03:11.572 --> 03:12.698
H-Huh?

03:16.410 --> 03:18.203
And who, pray tell, are you two?

03:18.579 --> 03:20.581
What are you up to?
Some kind of prank?

03:20.748 --> 03:22.416
N-No! We would never!

03:22.625 --> 03:25.294
Um, we go to
Budogaoka High School.

03:25.419 --> 03:27.462
W-We're your fans, Sensei.

03:27.588 --> 03:29.548
Fans? Of me?
You've read my stuff?

03:30.382 --> 03:31.466
So somebody leaked my address…

03:31.759 --> 03:35.179
N-No, um…
I just happened to hear…

03:35.596 --> 03:37.556
Pardon our rudeness,

03:37.640 --> 03:40.851
but nothing would make us
happier than your autograph.

03:40.935 --> 03:42.728
So you're fans, huh?

03:43.103 --> 03:44.020
Tremendous.

03:44.438 --> 03:46.022
We just might be
on the same wavelength, then.

03:46.524 --> 03:46.982
Huh?

03:47.066 --> 03:49.526
Nothing, never mind. Pardon me.

03:50.277 --> 03:53.571
An autograph or two
will be no trouble at all.

03:55.115 --> 03:57.117
Yes! Aren't you glad we came?

03:58.410 --> 03:59.285
I know.

03:59.787 --> 04:02.164
While you're here, I could
give you a studio tour if you'd like.

04:02.248 --> 04:02.957
Huh?

04:03.040 --> 04:05.167
We can see where you work?!

04:05.334 --> 04:07.044
My work is done for the day.

04:07.837 --> 04:09.171
If you two are interested…

04:09.255 --> 04:10.256
Yes!

04:10.464 --> 04:11.214
Then…

04:11.799 --> 04:13.509
'Souse us!

04:22.852 --> 04:23.978
Please.

04:24.103 --> 04:26.855
Wow!

04:31.318 --> 04:33.445
Wow! A four-color manuscript!

04:34.154 --> 04:37.615
Incredible!
It's so much more powerful in person!

04:37.825 --> 04:39.785
I-I'm overwhelmed!

04:39.910 --> 04:42.704
Thank god we came!

04:42.872 --> 04:45.875
How long have you
been practicing your craft in Morioh?

04:46.166 --> 04:48.084
I moved here three months ago.

04:48.502 --> 04:50.170
My family's home is in S City,

04:50.421 --> 04:53.590
but I used to live here
when I was a child.

04:53.841 --> 04:56.093
Tokyo has its perks,
but it's too chaotic for me.

04:56.844 --> 05:00.681
It has none of Morioh's serenity,
and is entirely unconducive to creativity.

05:01.348 --> 05:02.098
Besides,

05:02.182 --> 05:04.434
with today's advanced
fax machines and photocopiers,

05:04.852 --> 05:09.352
I can send a complete
manuscript in four hours.

05:09.940 --> 05:12.442
You could say there's no point
in living in the city now,

05:12.526 --> 05:14.236
other than for the pettiness of status.

05:14.361 --> 05:18.239
Um… And what do you do
about assistants and staff?

05:18.657 --> 05:20.575
I have none.
I draw everything myself.

05:20.826 --> 05:22.702
Huh? You do everything solo?!

05:22.828 --> 05:25.413
You draw 19 pages of those
intricate drawings in one week?!

05:25.623 --> 05:27.249
- I can do it in four.
- What?!

05:27.333 --> 05:28.375
Five if they're in color.

05:28.459 --> 05:31.128
On the other days,
I amuse myself with travel and such.

05:31.462 --> 05:33.172
I'm not much of a people person,

05:33.380 --> 05:35.131
which is why I chose
to be a manga artist.

05:35.716 --> 05:38.260
An assistant would be
a worry and a hindrance.

05:38.552 --> 05:40.345
That's so amazing… Wow.

05:40.429 --> 05:42.305
You're a genius!

05:42.723 --> 05:43.598
Excuse me.

05:43.891 --> 05:44.975
Whoa, a s-spider!

05:48.354 --> 05:49.730
Suburbia never ceases to amaze.

05:49.897 --> 05:51.481
The bugs and spiders are everywhere.

05:53.067 --> 05:54.943
Um… Sensei?

05:55.319 --> 05:58.488
I see… So this spider is
an <i>Araneus ventricosus…</i>

05:58.739 --> 06:01.241
The species inhabits homes
and rural areas across Japan.

06:01.575 --> 06:03.034
It's primarily an orb-weaving spider,

06:03.744 --> 06:06.621
and some weave webs day and night.

06:07.581 --> 06:08.748
By the way, you two,

06:09.041 --> 06:12.377
do you know what it takes
to create captivating manga?

06:13.754 --> 06:14.963
Reality!

06:15.381 --> 06:18.634
Reality is the force
that makes a drawing come alive.

06:18.759 --> 06:21.470
Reality is entertainment.

06:21.762 --> 06:25.056
People assume manga is
born of imagination and fantasy,

06:25.140 --> 06:27.058
but nothing could
be further from the truth!

06:27.142 --> 06:30.770
For me, it is capturing the seen,
the experienced, the felt,

06:30.938 --> 06:32.648
that makes for great manga!

06:34.608 --> 06:35.775
Take this spider…

06:35.859 --> 06:39.487
Something a typical city-dweller
would simply kill in disgust.

06:39.989 --> 06:43.325
The way the legs connect
to the body, the position of its eyes,

06:43.575 --> 06:46.077
the differences
between male and female.

06:46.286 --> 06:49.706
A manga artist must understand
these elements to draw a spider.

06:50.416 --> 06:54.294
It's said a spider's silk
solidifies when exposed to air,

06:54.628 --> 06:56.671
but what about its spinnerets?

06:57.381 --> 07:00.926
And then, there's the arrangement
of its internal organs.

07:01.301 --> 07:03.344
How does a spider
whose belly has been sliced open

07:03.595 --> 07:05.972
squirm in agony
while in the throes of death?

07:06.765 --> 07:10.059
To depict reality,
one must know such things.

07:11.186 --> 07:12.228
That's barbaric!

07:12.438 --> 07:13.188
Barbaric?!

07:13.480 --> 07:16.316
An amateur punk like you is
telling me, Rohan Kishibe, his opinion?!

07:17.484 --> 07:20.653
N-No! I wasn't voicing my opinion!
I'm sorry!

07:21.905 --> 07:23.531
Now for a taste.

07:27.161 --> 07:31.661
<i>The stereotype is true.
Manga artists really are total weirdos!</i>

07:33.834 --> 07:36.211
Very nice!
An excellent expression of agony…

07:36.336 --> 07:38.046
A perfect example
of the vomiting reflex!

07:38.464 --> 07:39.548
I must sketch it.

07:39.798 --> 07:41.549
R-Really?

07:47.097 --> 07:48.932
Now you're pretending.

07:50.100 --> 07:51.518
Forget it. No sketch.

07:51.685 --> 07:53.019
It won't be of any use.

07:53.270 --> 07:55.021
I-I'm sorry.

07:56.065 --> 07:57.441
Autographs, correct?

07:57.524 --> 07:59.984
I'll go get a pen from the kitchen.

08:00.194 --> 08:01.737
I'll bring out some tea, as well.

08:02.029 --> 08:03.530
Oh, you don't have to…

08:06.283 --> 08:08.576
That was amazing! I had no idea…

08:08.911 --> 08:11.204
That need to know every little detail

08:11.580 --> 08:14.749
must be what makes
<i>Pink Dark Boy</i> so amazing.

08:15.292 --> 08:16.626
Um, Hazamada…

08:17.878 --> 08:19.921
I know we just got here, but, um…

08:20.255 --> 08:23.383
Maybe, shouldn't we get going?

08:23.717 --> 08:25.510
Huh? Get going?
You want to go home? Why?

08:25.719 --> 08:27.262
Aren't you having fun?

08:27.513 --> 08:30.682
I can't really say why, but…

08:30.974 --> 08:32.934
It's just a feeling.

08:33.227 --> 08:35.938
My gut has been
known to be wrong…

08:36.146 --> 08:39.941
I just got the feeling there's something
dangerous about Rohan-sensei.

08:40.109 --> 08:41.276
Dangerous?

08:41.443 --> 08:44.529
You mean
he might be a Stand user?

08:44.863 --> 08:48.616
No! Nothing like that. Just, um…

08:48.742 --> 08:52.454
Just because Rohan-Sensei's
kind of off-the-wall,

08:52.579 --> 08:55.957
doesn't mean you should jump to
the conclusion that he's a Stand user.

08:56.250 --> 08:58.460
I'm not jumping to any conclusion…

08:58.585 --> 09:00.420
I just have a bad feeling.

09:00.504 --> 09:04.341
Besides, if Rohan-sensei
really is a Stand user,

09:04.508 --> 09:06.551
wouldn't that be great for us?

09:06.677 --> 09:10.847
We'd have something in common
with a famous manga artist.

09:10.931 --> 09:12.641
But, I feel you.

09:12.850 --> 09:14.726
If something's making you
feel weird,

09:14.810 --> 09:16.770
then that means it's time to go home.

09:17.104 --> 09:18.522
We can always come back.

09:19.106 --> 09:19.856
But!

09:20.190 --> 09:23.026
Only after I've looked at this thing
that caught my eye.

09:23.193 --> 09:25.737
Thing? What thing?

09:25.863 --> 09:28.156
Jeez, Koichi, could you
be any more dense?

09:28.448 --> 09:31.159
On top of the desk,
next to the phone.

09:31.410 --> 09:33.078
Look carefully.

09:39.877 --> 09:41.837
Oh! C-Could this be…

09:42.129 --> 09:43.338
Better believe it!

09:43.422 --> 09:45.465
He said he just
finished working, right?

09:45.632 --> 09:48.343
I've been eyeing that carefully.

09:48.719 --> 09:52.848
A freshly drawn, brand-spanking
new manuscript for <i>Pink Dark Boy?!</i>

09:53.140 --> 09:55.851
Does that mean
no one else has laid eyes on it?!

09:56.226 --> 09:58.645
We'll go home
as soon as I get a glimpse of this.

09:58.770 --> 10:01.022
We have to get Sensei's permission!

10:01.148 --> 10:04.359
Koichi, you really don't know anything
about manga artists, do you?

10:04.693 --> 10:07.028
These pre-printed manuscripts

10:07.154 --> 10:10.407
are highly confidential and top secret!

10:10.490 --> 10:12.783
There's no way
he'd let outsiders like us

10:12.951 --> 10:15.578
look at a manuscript
before the editor!

10:15.662 --> 10:17.705
We'll take a peak,
then put it right back.

10:17.831 --> 10:19.457
All the more reason!

10:19.666 --> 10:22.585
It's fine!
It's not gonna cause any harm.

10:29.885 --> 10:31.011
Huh?

10:34.598 --> 10:36.600
This feeling!

10:36.725 --> 10:40.937
I know it's a thrilling manga,
but seeing it in person like this…

10:41.104 --> 10:43.022
It's giving me goosebumps!

10:43.690 --> 10:45.108
It's so good!

10:45.275 --> 10:47.860
Hurry up and turn the page,
Hazamada.

10:48.070 --> 10:50.030
I'm getting emotional!

10:50.113 --> 10:51.405
It appears…

10:51.615 --> 10:56.115
my manuscript was compatible
with you two, after all.

10:56.536 --> 10:58.246
I thought you would read it.

10:58.664 --> 11:03.164
Only compatible first-time
readers of my manuscript…

11:04.962 --> 11:06.755
H-Hazamada…

11:06.880 --> 11:08.089
K-Koichi…

11:08.215 --> 11:11.134
…will experience with
my Heaven's Door ability,

11:11.218 --> 11:13.428
the very doors to their souls opening!

11:13.553 --> 11:15.346
A-Ability?!

11:16.890 --> 11:18.224
My hand!

11:23.272 --> 11:26.608
K-Koichi! What's going on?!

11:31.947 --> 11:35.951
MORIOH LANDMARK 5
MANGA ARTIST ROHAN KISHIBE'S HOUSE
ONE MINUTE WALK FROM
MORIOH KOTODAI 2-CHOME BUS STOP.
AN APPROXIMATELY 3,665 SQUARE-FOOT,
SEVEN ROOM MANSION WITH AN ATTIC.
IF YOU VISIT,
HE'LL PRETEND TO BE OUT.

11:36.493 --> 11:40.413
Many things are recorded
in the human body.

11:40.622 --> 11:42.957
Everything from the moment
you were born.

11:43.083 --> 11:46.711
To read your records,
I shall transform you both into books.

11:46.920 --> 11:49.964
Books that chronicle your life stories.

11:51.925 --> 11:55.303
- Help!
- You read the manga too, didn't you?

11:59.308 --> 12:00.851
- It's happening to me, too!
- Hazamada!

12:01.184 --> 12:04.270
This will cause you no physical harm,
so there's no need to worry.

12:04.563 --> 12:07.232
Wh-What do you want from us?!

12:07.482 --> 12:11.982
In manga, the creator's
sense of reality is critical, remember?

12:12.779 --> 12:16.449
That is, I will read your lives
and experiences,

12:16.533 --> 12:20.119
and you will flood
my consciousness with realistic ideas.

12:20.370 --> 12:22.330
An interview cannot do the same!

12:22.622 --> 12:26.417
You will tell me everything
with 100% realism,

12:26.501 --> 12:28.961
as if I had experienced it myself.

12:29.254 --> 12:33.549
Koichi Hirose.
Born March 28th, 1984, at 6:27 AM

12:33.633 --> 12:37.845
at Red Cross Hospital in S City.

12:38.221 --> 12:42.225
You were born premature at 2325 grams,
and spent a week in an incubator.

12:43.101 --> 12:45.353
You come from a family of four,
and your older sister's name is Ayana…

12:45.979 --> 12:46.771
I see…

12:47.147 --> 12:51.526
In grade school and middle school
you led a relatively ordinary life,

12:52.027 --> 12:54.696
you also happen to
be remarkably genuine.

12:54.905 --> 12:56.197
Admirable indeed.

12:58.867 --> 13:00.076
You…

13:00.160 --> 13:03.955
And what is this ability?! Reverb?

13:05.123 --> 13:09.127
So I am not alone in having
this kind of ability?!

13:09.544 --> 13:10.670
You, too?

13:15.008 --> 13:17.343
So Stand users… This is…

13:17.511 --> 13:21.556
Everything after
April, 1999 is astonishing!

13:21.681 --> 13:24.308
I see a sudden
explosion of amazing experiences!

13:24.476 --> 13:27.228
Josuke Higashikata, Jotaro Kujo,

13:27.354 --> 13:31.066
Yukako Yamagishi, Okuyasu
Nijimura, Tamami Kobayashi…

13:31.650 --> 13:32.859
It's unbelievable…

13:33.068 --> 13:35.028
It's incredible! It's captivating!

13:35.112 --> 13:39.612
I just uncovered the motherlode
of manga material, Koichi Hirose!

13:40.742 --> 13:42.577
Shining Diamond,

13:43.078 --> 13:44.496
Star Platinum,

13:44.746 --> 13:49.246
The Hand, Love Deluxe,
et cetera, et cetera!

13:49.960 --> 13:53.838
Wh-What are you gonna do with us?!

13:53.964 --> 13:56.049
I'm taking your memories

13:56.133 --> 13:58.677
to use in my own manga!

13:58.802 --> 13:59.844
Reverb!

14:02.973 --> 14:06.726
I'm asking you to stop attacking us
with your Stand this instant!

14:07.477 --> 14:08.227
Otherwise…

14:09.729 --> 14:13.274
You'll attack me with
Reverb Act 2's sound?

14:14.651 --> 14:18.112
Yes! Release me from your Stand!

14:18.238 --> 14:19.864
I won't hold back!

14:19.948 --> 14:24.448
I know. It's written on page eleven.

14:24.870 --> 14:29.370
You're far more timid than most,
and many tend to disrespect you,

14:30.292 --> 14:31.376
but when push comes to shove,

14:31.460 --> 14:34.087
you have the courage
to conquer your fears.

14:34.379 --> 14:35.421
Truly magnificent!

14:35.505 --> 14:36.964
I like you!

14:37.257 --> 14:40.843
I'm sure my readers
will like you, too.

14:41.011 --> 14:44.347
I'm not bluffing!
I will attack you!

14:44.431 --> 14:46.516
Oh, be quiet…

14:46.600 --> 14:48.143
Try me!

14:48.268 --> 14:49.686
Reverb Act 2!

14:53.356 --> 14:55.649
CRASH

14:56.067 --> 14:58.152
CRASH

14:56.985 --> 14:58.174
Huh? I-I missed?!

14:59.488 --> 15:03.366
I'm not sure you missed.
You sure it wasn't on purpose?

15:03.492 --> 15:06.161
Your control is way off!

15:06.786 --> 15:09.122
Then how about this?!

15:08.705 --> 15:09.580
CRASH

15:09.664 --> 15:10.414
CRASH

15:11.082 --> 15:13.292
Where are you attacking?!

15:13.418 --> 15:17.918
Koichi, unfortunately for you,
I placed a safety lock on Reverb.

15:18.882 --> 15:19.632
Huh?

15:19.966 --> 15:23.803
You are no longer able to attack me.

15:24.304 --> 15:26.180
Safety lock?

15:29.851 --> 15:34.351
Look… I've already written it into
the margin of page eleven, here.

15:37.192 --> 15:40.403
I CANNOT ATTACK
MANGA ARTIST, ROHAN KISHIBE

15:40.487 --> 15:43.072
I CANNOT ATTACK
MANGA ARTIST, ROHAN KISHIBE.

15:43.156 --> 15:47.285
CANNOT

15:47.327 --> 15:50.246
Behold, the power of Heaven's Door.

15:50.664 --> 15:52.707
Through it, I can read people's
experiences via words and pictures.

15:52.791 --> 15:55.919
Conversely, I can write in new memories.

15:56.169 --> 15:58.588
No matter what you try,

15:58.672 --> 16:01.591
you'll never be able to do me
any harm now.

16:02.008 --> 16:03.968
Wh-What?!

16:09.558 --> 16:12.561
But that's it. No more tampering.

16:12.727 --> 16:17.148
Any more, and your life
will lose all authenticity.

16:17.524 --> 16:19.901
It's of no benefit to my work.

16:20.527 --> 16:24.239
Now let's see…
Let's have a look at Hazamada.

16:24.364 --> 16:28.076
Sensei! You are a genius!
I respect you!

16:28.201 --> 16:29.911
Huh… I see.

16:30.287 --> 16:31.329
Let's see…

16:31.538 --> 16:35.458
You sometimes find comfort in
picking on the weak,

16:35.542 --> 16:38.086
like kittens and small birds.

16:38.503 --> 16:41.756
You want to have your way
with Junko, a junior from class E,

16:41.965 --> 16:43.925
but you're too cowardly
to act on that desire.

16:44.676 --> 16:46.302
Your testicles often grow sweaty,

16:46.469 --> 16:48.387
and when you adjust them
during class,

16:48.555 --> 16:51.891
nothing thrills you more than
the thought that someone might see you.

16:52.767 --> 16:54.393
You're an appalling excuse of a man.

16:54.561 --> 16:57.772
Including such a character
into my manga would turn off readers.

16:58.356 --> 16:59.648
I can't use you.

17:02.944 --> 17:04.487
This is too much!

17:04.738 --> 17:06.281
- Why?
- There's no hope for me!

17:07.741 --> 17:08.825
Why are you doing this?

17:09.409 --> 17:11.369
You don't need my experiences.

17:11.453 --> 17:14.372
You're amazing manga artist
on your own!

17:14.748 --> 17:16.833
The world knows that!

17:16.916 --> 17:20.127
You're only twenty years old,
and you live in this amazing house!

17:20.295 --> 17:22.797
Think of how blessed you are compared
with most people your age!

17:22.881 --> 17:26.342
So why do you need my memories?!

17:27.761 --> 17:31.306
Do you think that I,
Rohan Kishibe, draw manga

17:31.389 --> 17:33.599
to garner money and admiration?!

17:35.018 --> 17:37.937
I draw manga so
that people will read it!

17:38.188 --> 17:40.565
To be read is my only motive!

17:40.815 --> 17:44.777
It's only a single, simple reason,
but it's all I care about!

17:45.236 --> 17:49.736
So people read my work,
I search for realism every single day!

17:50.283 --> 17:54.287
Listen. Finishing a manuscript
always makes me feel good.

17:54.454 --> 17:57.582
Everyone feels good after
finishing work, don't they?

17:57.707 --> 18:00.459
But that gratification is fleeting.

18:00.877 --> 18:02.003
That's because,

18:02.212 --> 18:05.924
I begin to think
no one will read my manga,

18:06.174 --> 18:08.885
and my insecurities are awakened.

18:09.386 --> 18:11.805
Maybe next week
there will be no readers, I think…

18:11.888 --> 18:15.224
Maybe I won't know
what to draw anymore.

18:15.517 --> 18:18.686
Maybe I'll lose all motivation.

18:21.314 --> 18:24.066
These recurring thoughts
have tormented me

18:24.150 --> 18:26.277
over and over since I was sixteen.

18:26.444 --> 18:30.364
Until three months ago,
when someone shot me with an arrow,

18:30.490 --> 18:33.326
and I gained the ability of Heaven's Door.

18:33.493 --> 18:35.369
Keicho Nijimura…

18:35.453 --> 18:37.830
Yes, that was also written in you.

18:37.997 --> 18:41.000
I'm sure you two have no idea
what it's like to find

18:41.126 --> 18:43.461
the perfect inspiration
for a masterpiece!

18:43.628 --> 18:45.171
But this is it!

18:45.547 --> 18:46.673
There's nothing better!

18:46.840 --> 18:51.340
Koichi, I'm going to make
your reality mine!

19:06.192 --> 19:09.820
See, Koichi?
Wasn't Rohan-sensei a nice guy?

19:09.988 --> 19:11.364
Aren't you glad we went?

19:11.740 --> 19:13.700
It really was fun!

19:13.908 --> 19:15.409
TO HIROSE
ROHAN KISHIBE

19:14.033 --> 19:15.431
Not only did he give us
these great autographs,

19:16.536 --> 19:18.788
he even served us tea and cookies.

19:18.913 --> 19:20.789
I wanna go back.

19:20.915 --> 19:23.125
Yeah. Let's go again.

19:23.668 --> 19:25.461
Well, I'm heading this way, so…

19:27.046 --> 19:29.590
He really was a great guy.

19:38.516 --> 19:42.603
You'll never speak of this, Koichi.

19:45.565 --> 19:46.440
Huh?!

19:46.566 --> 19:48.150
Wh-Why?!

19:48.276 --> 19:51.112
How did I lose 20 kilograms?

19:53.364 --> 19:55.783
But I look exactly the same!

19:57.494 --> 19:59.245
It reads five kilograms…

19:59.412 --> 20:00.996
The scale's not broken.

20:04.459 --> 20:06.419
Th-This is crazy!

20:06.586 --> 20:09.338
Th-This has to be the work
of an enemy Stand!

20:09.881 --> 20:13.009
There's no other way
I'd lose 20 kilograms!

20:13.176 --> 20:14.677
But who…

20:14.886 --> 20:17.346
I have to talk to Josuke about this.

20:20.600 --> 20:22.351
Ko, what are you doing?

20:22.685 --> 20:23.477
Huh?

20:24.270 --> 20:26.647
Me? U-Uh…

20:26.981 --> 20:28.857
Wait… What was it?

20:29.108 --> 20:31.193
What are you talking about?
Weirdo.

20:31.402 --> 20:32.403
<i>What's wrong?</i>

20:32.487 --> 20:36.282
Oh, nothing. My little brother's
wandering around in his underwear.

20:36.366 --> 20:37.825
What was it?

20:38.243 --> 20:42.372
I could've sworn I was thinking about
something really important just now.

20:46.042 --> 20:49.879
Well, if I forgot that easily,
it couldn't have been that important.

20:54.509 --> 20:59.009
Boy, my shoes and bag
sure feel heavy today.

20:59.722 --> 21:00.472
Huh?

21:02.141 --> 21:04.143
<i>Th-This house…</i>

21:04.435 --> 21:05.602
<i>Why?</i>

21:05.687 --> 21:09.982
<i>Somehow I ended up
walking to Rohan-Sensei's house.</i>

21:11.651 --> 21:13.194
<i>The door's open…</i>

21:13.319 --> 21:16.280
<i>I'd like to drop in
and thank him for yesterday,</i>

21:16.573 --> 21:20.868
<i>but I'll be late for school.
I probably shouldn't.</i>

21:21.661 --> 21:24.413
<i>Being a manga artist,
he'll probably still be asleep.</i>

21:24.664 --> 21:26.874
<i>I really shouldn't just barge in.</i>

21:27.792 --> 21:29.627
<i>This really isn't such a good idea…</i>

21:37.051 --> 21:39.386
Hey, did you see that, Okuyasu?

21:39.512 --> 21:40.554
Yeah…

21:40.847 --> 21:43.641
We followed Koichi because
he was heading in

21:43.766 --> 21:47.436
the opposite direction of the school,
but what the heck is he doing?

21:47.562 --> 21:49.772
Whose house is that?

21:49.939 --> 21:52.691
There's no way but,
you don't think it's some chick, do ya?

22:05.330 --> 22:06.914
<i>Rohan-sensei..</i>

22:08.166 --> 22:10.877
<i>He's working with
such a chilling expression.</i>

22:11.002 --> 22:12.336
<i>What is this…</i>

22:12.420 --> 22:16.132
<i>I can't shake the feeling that
being here is actually terrifying.</i>

22:16.257 --> 22:17.883
<i>What is it?</i>

22:18.509 --> 22:19.718
So you made it.

22:20.136 --> 22:22.429
I've been waiting.
You're right on time.

23:39.382 --> 23:42.426
EPISODE 15
LET'S GO TO
THE MANGA ARTIST'S HOUSE, PART 2
